STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece looks like a gifted schoolboy's drawing on a page of a Chinese school exercise book of the 1990s: confident blue ballpoint pen outlines, soft coloured pencil hatching and shading, a little graphite, on off-white exercise paper with faint pale blue ruled lines across it. Warm and lively, with friendly faces drawn with care. Bold, clear shapes that read from the back row. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: exercise paper #F3F0E6, ballpoint blue #2F3F8F, pencil grey #6A6A6A, tracksuit blue #3C6DB4, tracksuit white #F5F5F0, court orange #D9874A, plane-tree green #6E9A4C, dusk gold #E8B25A, brick red #B5523E, with raw card brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is warm, nostalgic and bittersweet.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no characters, no letters, no numbers, no Chinese characters, no writing on boards, books, envelopes or signs, no logos, no slogans, no flags, no red scarves, no badges, no signature, no watermark. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish, no anime style.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its ballpoint outlines, coloured pencil hatching, ruled exercise paper, palette, raw card edges and figure style. Do not copy its composition.
SUBJECT: The four pieces of a marionette of Xiaoyu, a grown Chinese man in his thirties, facing three-quarters to the right: (1) the head with short black hair, a gentle tired face with a soft smile, and the bare neck; (2) the body from the neck base down to dark leather shoes, a dark grey work jacket open over a white shirt with no tie, dark trousers, standing, with NO arms; (3) his RIGHT arm from shoulder to an open hand, dark sleeve; (4) his LEFT arm from shoulder to a hand holding a small old dented round biscuit tin, dark sleeve.
COMPOSITION: A flat lay of the separate cardboard pieces of ONE jointed puppet, all at the same scale, seen straight from the front on a transparent background. Each piece is a separate cutout with clear empty space around it. No piece touches or overlaps another piece. No shadow, no rod, no strings, no stand, no stage.
JOINTS: The body has three clearly visible round brass split pins: one at the centre of the base of the neck and one on each shoulder. The body ends at the neck base with no head and has no arms. The head piece ends in a bare neck with no collar, with one brass pin at the bottom of the neck. Each arm piece has one brass pin at the very top of the shoulder. One arm is a RIGHT arm and the other is a LEFT arm, with the thumbs on the correct sides. The head is drawn at a natural size for the body.
